{"id":43,"flavor":[{"games":["Shield","X","Crystal"],"text":"During the day, it stays in the cold underground to avoid the sun. It grows by bathing in moonlight."},{"games":["Sword","SoulSilver","Silver"],"text":"If exposed to moonlight, it starts to move. It roams far and wide at night to scatter its seeds."},{"games":["Let’s Go, Eevee!","Let’s Go, Pikachu!","Yellow"],"text":"It may be mistaken for a clump of weeds. If you try to yank it out of the ground, it shrieks horribly."},{"games":["Alpha Sapphire","Sapphire"],"text":"Oddish searches for fertile, nutrient-rich soil, then plants itself. During the daytime, while it is planted, this Pokémon’s feet are thought to change shape and become similar to the roots of trees."},{"games":["Omega Ruby","Ruby"],"text":"During the daytime, Oddish buries itself in soil to absorb nutrients from the ground using its entire body. The more fertile the soil, the glossier its leaves become."},{"games":["Y","FireRed"],"text":"Its scientific name is “Oddium Wanderus.” At night, it is said to walk nearly 1,000 feet on its two roots."},{"games":["White 2","Black 2","White","Black","Platinum","Pearl","Diamond"],"text":"It often plants its root feet in the ground during the day and sows seeds as it walks about at night."},{"games":["HeartGold","Gold"],"text":"Awakened by moonlight, it roams actively at night. In the day, it stays quietly underground."},{"games":["LeafGreen","Blue","Red"],"text":"During the day, it keeps its face buried in the ground. At night, it wanders around sowing its seeds."},{"games":["Emerald"],"text":"This POKéMON grows by absorbing moonlight. During the daytime, it buries itself in the ground, leaving only its leaves exposed to avoid detection by its enemies."}],"abilities":[{"name":"Chlorophyll","hidden":false,"description":"Boosts the Pokémon's Speed stat in harsh sunlight."},{"name":"Run Away","hidden":true,"description":"Enables a sure getaway from wild Pokémon."}],"eggGroups":["Grass"],"genderRate":4,"hatc